## Android native interface

The Android APK uses AndroidX Compose/Material3, Activity, Lifecycle, Kotlin,
kotlinx.coroutines, and their runtime dependencies. Their retained Apache-2.0,
ThreeTen BSD-3-Clause, and Boost-1.0 notices are in
`android/OPEN_SOURCE_NOTICES`, bundled alongside this document and accessible
from Settings > Open-source notices. The native Rust/Go components below keep
their existing licenses. Flutter and its interface packages are not included
in the native Android APK.

## Country names and flag rendering

Bundled flag images and English/Russian country labels render offline on both
desktop platforms. The Android APK bundles the same country data and flag
images, exported from country_flags as WebP files; the flag artwork comes from
flag-icons. Package license texts are retained below and in Flutter’s
generated license asset.

